lection" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423297 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423284 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423297 1079 #uuid "6361ce30-11cc-5a0d-850d-da69a68b03ec" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423298 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423285 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423298 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423287 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423298 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423288 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423298 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423291 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423298 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423295 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423298 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423298 1077 "selection" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423298 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423288 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423298 1079 #uuid "66bbcaef-4127-5612-b288-bf682df65c65" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423299 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423298 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423299 1069 "q-90877" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423299 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423299 1071 "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+9y=0.$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution to the equation, then $\\lambda =$" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423299 1072 #uuid "47a2dcc0-e258-5962-a656-0d85d7377a49" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423299 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+9{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -3)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =3$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation." 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423300 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423296 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423300 1069 "q-130137" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423300 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423300 1071 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=0.\n$$" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423300 1072 #uuid "b7f674b2-aab8-52eb-92a0-8e6f21742e6b" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423300 1074 "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -1)^{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =1$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x}.\n$$" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423301 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423297 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423301 1069 "q-90967" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423301 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423301 1071 "Given the equation ${y}^{″}-10{y}^{′}+25y=0$ for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423301 1072 #uuid "f8f7ce6d-af6c-546a-90a8-f18d93a76742" 13194139534503 17592186045417 true] [17592186423301 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-10\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+25{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -5)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =5$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{5x}$ and $x{e}^{5x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{5x}-5{e}^{x}$ is not a solution." 13194139534503 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-166df338-5ee1-5ac6-aaaa-9ca285549f5a" 17592186423281 "answer-46cbbb4c-cb47-543a-acd8-7156e51b12bc" 17592186423282 "answer-47c4a9bf-3526-5449-afb6-bee6b3f978ef" 17592186423283 "answer-47d65475-b294-5939-87f4-976439c24d81" 17592186423284 "answer-5dfe0d35-2b45-549e-9933-eda97f80460e" 17592186423285 "answer-8417cb9c-2a17-5b03-ae26-d7eed71a77d6" 17592186423286 "answer-a53e8e73-9688-515a-b743-c06ba5034590" 17592186423287 "answer-a6605268-308f-5aa9-8a2b-aea33ea5ec54" 17592186423288 "answer-a95b7289-0f33-518d-a65d-3efd954fb420" 17592186423289 "answer-b4c81132-c41c-5bf0-99f6-631bbb43fd38" 17592186423290 "answer-c6fb89a7-9365-52c1-965f-ef6f3b099aef" 17592186423291 "answer-e0d39602-f1f5-5e9f-a832-afc75a851baf" 17592186423292 "answer-ef346c19-c04f-532b-9394-8e47cdeef76c" 17592186423293 "answer-f211fd22-4438-5855-a248-834360be2359" 17592186423294 "answer-f9ccba15-05c7-5